    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1092">

                <pb facs="0962" n="858" xml:id="pg858"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/9620.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to
                            Germany to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-11-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 8, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your November 7, 10 p.m. The Foreign Office states that Germany has no political
                    interest in the subject but that Mexico must have order and responsible
                    government and wishes to know what candidate for the presidency we have.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gerard</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
